WEBVTT

00:00:02.100 --> 00:00:04.350
It is nice to make your acquaintance,
Mahmut Bey.

00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:07.730
I am the kulak, Kiros.

00:00:07.900 --> 00:00:11.070
No nation has ever defeated the Balt-Rhein Empire!

00:00:11.280 --> 00:00:16.070
However, it was Mahmut Pasha there who showed
the world it was not impossible in Hisar!

00:00:16.320 --> 00:00:18.450
Is this the reason I was brought here?

00:00:19.830 --> 00:00:21.290
I address the nation!

00:00:21.450 --> 00:00:25.330
In light of the Balt-Rhein Empire's aggressions
against our nation,

00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:27.750
Phoinike will take up arms to defend ourselves!

00:00:48.020 --> 00:00:51.400
Altair: A Record of Battles

00:02:03.140 --> 00:02:04.640
Kaisaras Apollodorus.

00:02:05.560 --> 00:02:09.440
Perhaps you could consider
contributing to the cause?

00:02:10.360 --> 00:02:14.690
Every citizen has taken up arms
to fight.

00:02:14.860 --> 00:02:18.910
While you may not have supported
this war,

00:02:19.070 --> 00:02:23.120
should you not be making the best of it as Kaisaras?

00:02:24.080 --> 00:02:28.620
Do you still believe this war was
the right decision, Magistros?

00:02:29.210 --> 00:02:31.130
You are still on about that?

00:02:34.300 --> 00:02:35.510
Of course I do!

00:02:36.380 --> 00:02:38.380
Did you not see?

00:02:38.550 --> 00:02:41.720
How the people under the Empire end up?

00:02:41.890 --> 00:02:44.430
If we joined the Empire,

00:02:44.640 --> 00:02:47.100
we would share the same fate.

00:02:48.180 --> 00:02:49.980
Even if that were the case,

00:02:50.100 --> 00:02:54.860
I still view this war as a mistake.

00:03:14.040 --> 00:03:16.420
The Iron Chains

00:03:17.210 --> 00:03:21.470
Tomorrow morning, we will launch our fifth attack
at the break of dawn.

00:03:22.050 --> 00:03:25.180
The Camino Fleet will head the seaside vanguard!

00:03:25.390 --> 00:03:28.350
The Coronia Fleet will lead the landside vanguard!

00:03:28.560 --> 00:03:30.690
How long is this going to continue?

00:03:31.350 --> 00:03:35.770
We've already failed four times!
This is ridiculous.

00:03:35.940 --> 00:03:41.030
We're going to be killed by the Imperials,
not the Phoinikian.

00:03:43.450 --> 00:03:45.200
Change lookouts!

00:03:45.990 --> 00:03:47.290
We attack tomorrow.

00:03:47.450 --> 00:03:50.750
Keep a close watch tonight
to make sure there are no deserters.

00:03:50.910 --> 00:03:51.910
Yes, sir!

00:03:55.290 --> 00:03:58.210
Water! We're taking in water!

00:04:24.490 --> 00:04:26.990
The look suits you, Mahmut Bey.

00:04:27.200 --> 00:04:32.710
Now even if we're caught, you'll be able
to die without bringing trouble to your country.

00:04:33.080 --> 00:04:36.750
I am not planning on making these
my burial garments.

00:04:37.500 --> 00:04:38.500
Kiros.

00:04:38.880 --> 00:04:42.050
Let us both make it out alive.

00:04:53.640 --> 00:04:55.060
Let's go.

00:04:56.600 --> 00:04:58.560
We'll be able to escape now.

00:04:59.320 --> 00:05:01.820
Epaminondas, did you get the weapons we need?

00:05:02.360 --> 00:05:03.610
All set!

00:05:03.820 --> 00:05:04.990
And food?

00:05:05.110 --> 00:05:06.780
Yeah, we managed to get it together.

00:05:06.950 --> 00:05:08.660
Getting this all together in one day,

00:05:08.830 --> 00:05:11.700
I never would've agreed to do it
for anyone but you, Kiros.

00:05:11.870 --> 00:05:13.910
Well, you really saved us.

00:05:14.080 --> 00:05:16.120
So you must be Mahmut Bey.

00:05:16.710 --> 00:05:18.080
Yes.

00:05:20.210 --> 00:05:26.380
I've come because I believed Kiros when he
said this voyage would put an end to this war.

00:05:27.050 --> 00:05:30.930
I'm not putting my life in your hands,
but in Kiros'.

00:05:31.100 --> 00:05:34.270
I'm not putting my life in anyone's hand!

00:05:34.430 --> 00:05:38.100
We've had our fair share of run-ins
with pirates!

00:05:38.270 --> 00:05:41.900
We could evade these Balt-Rhein ships
in our sleep!

00:05:42.440 --> 00:05:47.530
We need this war finished, or we won't
be able to get back to our own ship!

00:05:48.200 --> 00:05:51.910
These guys have more guts than any soldier.

00:05:52.620 --> 00:05:54.910
They're the kind of people you can rely on.

00:05:56.290 --> 00:05:59.170
I want to thank every one of you.

00:05:59.960 --> 00:06:02.170
We shall take this ship to Venedik

00:06:02.380 --> 00:06:06.470
and have them send reinforcements
as soon as possible.

00:06:08.300 --> 00:06:10.220
Now then, all that's left to do

00:06:10.430 --> 00:06:14.140
is to remove the harbor's chain over there
without being detected.

00:06:40.670 --> 00:06:41.830
Magistros!

00:06:42.460 --> 00:06:43.840
The enemy are coming!

00:06:46.670 --> 00:06:49.340
They're flying a crescent flag!

00:06:54.720 --> 00:06:58.600
In the name of Navalat,
mother spirit of the Centro,

00:06:59.190 --> 00:07:02.100
we offer our surrender to Phoinike.

00:07:02.900 --> 00:07:05.940
We humbly request safe haven.

00:07:06.610 --> 00:07:08.280
So that's their angle.

00:07:08.990 --> 00:07:10.450
This is surely a trap.

00:07:12.660 --> 00:07:14.660
What about your families?

00:07:14.830 --> 00:07:18.700
If you surrender to us, your families will surely
have to pay the price.

00:07:21.830 --> 00:07:25.960
We are miners from the old Camino Kingdom
located in northern Rhein

00:07:26.130 --> 00:07:28.920
that has been absorbed by the Empire.

00:07:29.090 --> 00:07:32.300
Five months ago, when we headed
to the coal mines as usual,

00:07:32.470 --> 00:07:35.850
the Imperial Army arrived and ordered us
into their carriages.

00:07:36.010 --> 00:07:37.390
Let's return to the ship.

00:07:38.020 --> 00:07:42.900
And we were brought here to this battleground
without being told anything.

00:07:43.100 --> 00:07:45.480
Camino winters are harsh.

00:07:46.480 --> 00:07:48.860
I can't imagine our families could have survived it

00:07:49.030 --> 00:07:51.860
after losing all the able-bodied men.

00:07:58.830 --> 00:08:00.370
The Imperial fleet?!

00:08:00.710 --> 00:08:03.170
Extinguish the torches, or we'll be easy targets!

00:08:03.330 --> 00:08:04.670
Damn it!

00:08:05.000 --> 00:08:07.250
So this is the way we're treated

00:08:07.420 --> 00:08:09.960
for our faithful service to the Empire?

00:08:10.760 --> 00:08:13.340
Please believe us, Lord Phoinikians!

00:08:13.550 --> 00:08:16.350
We surrender to you!

00:08:16.550 --> 00:08:19.810
-Go ahead and kill us, Balt-Rhein!
-Please!

00:08:19.970 --> 00:08:24.350
Phoinikians! We will fight alongside you!

00:08:24.560 --> 00:08:28.610
Please lower these chains!
We beg of you!

00:08:33.490 --> 00:08:36.200
I would like to let them in.

00:08:37.240 --> 00:08:40.830
There should be many like them
with the same dissatisfactions.

00:08:41.000 --> 00:08:43.040
If we allow them entry here,

00:08:43.210 --> 00:08:48.170
the Imperials will suffer a blow to morale,
and begin crumbling within the ranks.

00:08:49.460 --> 00:08:52.260
In honor of the Phoinikian Senate
traditions of old,

00:08:52.420 --> 00:08:55.470
I call this matter to an emergency vote.

00:08:58.470 --> 00:09:02.730
All in favor of taking in the deserters.

00:09:12.320 --> 00:09:14.360
The ayes have it.

00:09:14.530 --> 00:09:17.450
We will now take in the Imperial deserters.

00:09:18.990 --> 00:09:21.370
Zenon, how far are the Imperial ships?

00:09:22.330 --> 00:09:24.370
I'd say...

00:09:24.960 --> 00:09:27.370
They're about 800 ziras away.

00:09:27.580 --> 00:09:29.460
Nikephoros, what is the wind?

00:09:29.630 --> 00:09:33.300
It's a weak southern wind and the tides are high.

00:09:33.800 --> 00:09:36.840
Calculating all of this, the Imperial ships will arrive...

00:09:37.380 --> 00:09:39.510
in approximately 250 seconds.

00:09:39.680 --> 00:09:40.680
Can we do it?

00:09:40.850 --> 00:09:44.680
The pursuers are in sailing vessels with sea gauges
of roughly six to eight ziras.

00:09:44.850 --> 00:09:48.150
The deserters are in a galley ship.
Its sea gauge is four to six ziras.

00:09:48.310 --> 00:09:51.940
If we drop the chain down to six ziras,
the galley ship will be able to pass.

00:09:52.110 --> 00:09:54.690
It takes 20 seconds to lower the chain by one zira.

00:09:54.860 --> 00:09:59.410
It takes four times that to raise it.
If we raise the chain as soon as the galley passes,

00:09:59.570 --> 00:10:02.540
the Imperial ships will not be able to enter the harbor!

00:10:03.870 --> 00:10:07.580
Engine room! Lower the harbor chains immediately!

00:10:07.750 --> 00:10:10.750
We are letting the Imperial deserters enter!

00:10:10.960 --> 00:10:14.090
Raise the chains as soon
as the deserters make it through!

00:10:14.260 --> 00:10:15.300
Hurry!

00:10:24.470 --> 00:10:28.440
I repeat, we will allow the Imperial deserters entry.

00:10:28.600 --> 00:10:32.940
After the deserters pass through,
close off the harbor immediately!

00:10:34.020 --> 00:10:37.950
Witness us, Balt-Rhein, you false empire.

00:10:38.490 --> 00:10:45.620
To govern nations, you need the love
and pride of your citizens,

00:10:45.830 --> 00:10:49.000
just as it was with ancient Phoinike.

00:10:49.540 --> 00:10:55.130
Who would love a nation that would
dispose of you like pawns?

00:10:55.630 --> 00:10:59.220
Such a nation is doomed to fail.

00:11:00.300 --> 00:11:02.390
The galley ship has made it through!

00:11:02.600 --> 00:11:06.220
The galley ship has made it through!
Raise the chain! Hurry!

00:11:13.520 --> 00:11:14.610
What?

00:11:15.360 --> 00:11:19.150
Why is the center ship's sea gauge so shallow?

00:11:19.320 --> 00:11:22.530
Simply unloading all the cargo
wouldn't make it that shallow.

00:11:23.070 --> 00:11:25.660
That's three ziras, at the most!

00:11:25.830 --> 00:11:29.080
Wait! Did they cast off their ballasts?

00:11:29.250 --> 00:11:30.250
Ballasts?

00:11:30.410 --> 00:11:33.000
They're weights added to the ship's hull for stability.

00:11:33.170 --> 00:11:37.090
Removing the ballasts would normally cause a ship
to lose balance and capsize!

00:11:39.550 --> 00:11:43.680
It's tied to the two ships on either side!

00:11:45.390 --> 00:11:47.220
-Nikephoros!
-I'm on it!

00:11:51.480 --> 00:11:53.230
Twenty seconds.

00:11:54.190 --> 00:11:55.810
We won't make it in time.

00:12:00.440 --> 00:12:02.660
Engine room, use the water wheel!

00:12:02.820 --> 00:12:04.410
We can use it at high tide!

00:12:04.570 --> 00:12:07.030
That would be able to raise the chains faster!

00:12:07.200 --> 00:12:08.990
Hurry!

00:12:18.710 --> 00:12:20.010
We'll make it in time!

00:12:26.180 --> 00:12:29.180
Rende! It's the seasonal nautical wind!

00:12:29.390 --> 00:12:32.140
A tailwind... No...

00:12:35.900 --> 00:12:37.690
They're coming in on the tide as well.

00:12:37.860 --> 00:12:40.860
It seems the time and direction were all calculated.

00:12:41.030 --> 00:12:43.070
There's nothing we can do.

00:12:47.660 --> 00:12:49.330
Cut the ropes on both sides!

00:13:03.880 --> 00:13:05.800
Storeroom, now!

00:13:34.330 --> 00:13:37.460
The Imperial ship has broken through!

00:13:39.080 --> 00:13:40.920
Relay to all units stationed at the wall!

00:13:41.090 --> 00:13:44.670
All soldiers not on lookout
are to head to the harbor immediately!

00:13:45.420 --> 00:13:47.840
Only one enemy ship has broken through!

00:13:48.430 --> 00:13:50.680
Do not allow them to land!

00:13:51.470 --> 00:13:56.850
But none of the ships in the harbor
are ready to be launched...

00:13:57.940 --> 00:14:00.520
Then... Then...

00:14:00.730 --> 00:14:02.520
Take as many bows as you can!

00:14:02.690 --> 00:14:05.070
Line the archers along the wharf!

00:14:05.240 --> 00:14:07.860
The enemy is the Ellvaldes Mountain Troop!

00:14:08.030 --> 00:14:11.120
We have to stop them before they bring
the battle to land!

00:14:11.910 --> 00:14:16.080
Why did I not ready any ships?!

00:14:16.250 --> 00:14:19.210
Because for 3000 years this city
has been impregnable?

00:14:19.330 --> 00:14:25.380
That it would never be possible for this port to be taken
by the new and inexperienced Balt-Rhein Navy?!

00:14:26.340 --> 00:14:29.010
Am I a fool?!

00:14:32.810 --> 00:14:34.180
There's a ship!

00:14:34.430 --> 00:14:38.020
There's a ship charging the Imperial ship!

00:14:42.150 --> 00:14:44.940
-Are you all ready?!
-Yeah!

00:14:45.150 --> 00:14:46.740
Lord Glalat!

00:14:46.900 --> 00:14:49.320
It is not a problem.
It actually works in our favor.

00:14:49.490 --> 00:14:50.950
Let them ram us.

00:14:51.160 --> 00:14:54.620
Making it to land is not our objective.

00:14:54.790 --> 00:14:56.250
Go!

00:14:56.450 --> 00:14:59.000
Break a hole in their side!

00:15:10.970 --> 00:15:12.930
-They did it!
-They stopped it.

00:15:13.510 --> 00:15:17.060
Use this time to get the ships ready now!

00:15:17.390 --> 00:15:18.890
Shields up!

00:15:20.190 --> 00:15:22.440
Did we perform to your satisfaction, Mahmut Bey?

00:15:22.600 --> 00:15:23.730
You've exceeded them.

00:15:23.900 --> 00:15:26.690
One surprise attack deserves another.

00:15:47.340 --> 00:15:48.960
Let's go!

00:15:57.470 --> 00:15:59.560
-Is this all?
-There's someone collapsed here.

00:15:59.730 --> 00:16:02.020
-I'm on my way!
-Don't let your guard down.

00:16:02.310 --> 00:16:05.020
The elite Ellvaldes Mountain Troop.

00:16:05.940 --> 00:16:08.150
We would've been no match for them on land.

00:16:08.730 --> 00:16:12.150
-There should still be a lot more in the ship, Kiros.
-Yeah.

00:16:13.240 --> 00:16:15.030
Mahmut Bey.

00:16:15.240 --> 00:16:17.120
Please keep watch here.

00:16:17.280 --> 00:16:18.290
Okay.

00:16:18.450 --> 00:16:19.950
I'll stay here too.

00:16:45.100 --> 00:16:46.650
Nails?

00:16:48.730 --> 00:16:50.860
A militia would never dare to challenge

00:16:51.030 --> 00:16:55.950
the Empire's most elite unit,
the Ellvaldes Mountain Troop, head on.

00:16:57.200 --> 00:16:58.830
An eagle handler.

00:16:59.370 --> 00:17:01.290
You must be Mahmut of Torqye.

00:17:04.870 --> 00:17:08.290
Is he the Imperial emissary I walked past then?

00:17:37.160 --> 00:17:39.240
I was expecting more.

00:17:39.410 --> 00:17:42.580
You are able to coolly handle your enemies,

00:17:42.740 --> 00:17:44.580
but you would put yourself at risk

00:17:44.750 --> 00:17:46.620
to protect a useless ally.

00:17:50.130 --> 00:17:51.840
I'm disappointed.

00:17:55.170 --> 00:17:57.380
It's completely empty?

00:18:10.400 --> 00:18:11.520
Iskandar!

00:18:11.690 --> 00:18:13.900
He threw oil on his wings!

00:18:58.860 --> 00:19:04.370
Did you really think you could defeat us
with so few people?

00:19:04.490 --> 00:19:06.450
It seems like it's over.

00:19:06.620 --> 00:19:09.410
Don't worry, your lives will be spared.

00:19:09.580 --> 00:19:13.420
Phoinike guarantees the safety of their
prisoners of war.

00:19:13.630 --> 00:19:16.090
Yeah! Now, surrender!

00:19:18.220 --> 00:19:21.430
You'll spare our lives, will you?

00:19:22.220 --> 00:19:25.640
Living peacefully behind your castle walls,

00:19:25.850 --> 00:19:30.350
does that make you conceited enough
to protect the lives of your enemies?

00:19:31.060 --> 00:19:32.310
Maybe.

00:19:32.480 --> 00:19:34.150
But if you died,

00:19:34.270 --> 00:19:38.150
you would not be able to answer
for all of the lives you've taken.

00:19:41.410 --> 00:19:45.240
In our native home Ellvaldes,

00:19:45.450 --> 00:19:48.410
most of the land is made up
of barren mountains,

00:19:48.580 --> 00:19:52.710
and on top of that, it's at the mercy of winter
for over half of the year.

00:19:52.870 --> 00:19:56.800
It is an impoverished nation
where nothing can be grown.

00:19:56.960 --> 00:19:59.920
But by winning this battle,

00:20:00.090 --> 00:20:02.880
when Phoinike is made an Imperial territory,

00:20:03.050 --> 00:20:08.640
the Emperor will bestow us
with half of the lucrative revenue.

00:20:09.560 --> 00:20:12.560
Yes, that is what Minister Louis promised us.

00:20:13.400 --> 00:20:14.860
As I thought...

00:20:15.020 --> 00:20:16.150
Louis.

00:20:25.950 --> 00:20:28.870
The future of my homeland is at stake.

00:20:29.040 --> 00:20:31.330
We are willing to sacrifice our lives.

00:20:38.710 --> 00:20:39.840
Mahmut Bey!

00:20:53.520 --> 00:20:56.770
Why?! Something seems off.

00:20:58.980 --> 00:21:01.230
The winds are about to change.

00:21:03.990 --> 00:21:08.280
Three thousand years of history comes to an end.

00:21:27.140 --> 00:21:28.220
Kiros!

00:21:28.390 --> 00:21:29.760
The city!

00:21:29.930 --> 00:21:33.020
And now this nation is ours!

00:21:38.900 --> 00:21:41.730
I said I would have this settled

00:21:41.940 --> 00:21:44.530
by the time Orion caught the moon, but...

00:21:49.410 --> 00:21:53.200
Sorry I'm late.

00:21:53.830 --> 00:21:59.210
I guess they believed there weren't any holes
in their impregnable wall.

00:21:59.420 --> 00:22:03.710
Seems like they got dazzled
by the sparkle of the crystals.

00:22:04.970 --> 00:22:08.680
In any case, I had a good time.

00:23:48.400 --> 00:23:51.400
I can't figure out why he would
betray a friend.

00:23:51.570 --> 00:23:54.660
Or am I the one who's wrong?

00:23:55.660 --> 00:23:58.080
Next time, "The Sinking City."

00:23:58.200 --> 00:24:00.910
The shroud of doubt obscures the way.

00:24:01.080 --> 00:24:02.500
The Sinking City
